Name=Initial Level Unlocks
Description=Sets the level-select flags SelectLevelInit gives each arcade level when a new game starts. Each of the 15 calls SelectSetLevelFlags(level, flags) takes a level id (the FroggerMapLevelID ordinal, ORG1 = 24) and a flags value: 1 = completed, 2 = selectable, 4 = zone accessible, so 6 starts a level unlocked and 4 shows its world picture without letting it be played. The game assigns the flags (it does not combine them) and ignores levels missing from the arcade table, so repeating a pair is harmless. Retail gives 6 to ORG1, SUB1, FOR1 and VOL1 and 4 to ORG2-5, SUB2-5, FOR2, VOL2 and VOL3. The five multiplayer calls that follow are not touched. The PSX addresses come from the Frogger Plus+ script and were not verified against a PSX executable; the pc-retail-v3.0e-vogons addresses repeat the v3.0e ones, as that script does, and were not checked against that executable either.
Author=jimbolina
Versions=pc-retail-v3.0e,pc-retail-v3.0e-vogons,psx-retail-usa

